    {
      "id": "p0082-b007",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "The Japanese language has multiple words that can mean \"underground'', each with its own unique nuances. In Undertale's case, the localization team decided to translate \"Underground\" as chitei (\"depths of the earth\") and chitei no sekai (\"world at the depths of the earth\") as needed. In fiction, chitei tends to evoke the feeling of a vast underground land or realm of unseen wonders:",
        "raw": "The Japanese language has multiple words that can mean \"underground'', each\nwith its own unique nuances. In Underta/e's case, the localization team decided\nto translate \"Underground\" as chitei (\"depths of the earth\") and chitei no sekai\n(\"world at the depths of the earth\") as needed. In fiction, chitei tends to evoke\nthe feeling of a vast underground land or realm of unseen wonders:",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.2942778,
          0.41100714,
          0.90401505,
          0.49643571
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.29140053,
          0.41029286,
          0.90890233,
          0.49750714
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          15,
          16,
          17,
          18,
          19
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "日语里有几个词都能表示“地下”，各自又带着不同的细微含义。本地化团队为 Undertale 选择了 chitei（地底）和 chitei no sekai（地底世界），视语境使用。在虚构作品中，chitei 往往让人想到辽阔的地下大陆，或藏着未知奇观的世界：",
        "status": "draft",
