    {
      "id": "p0082-b010",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "On a side note, the decision to use chitei in the Japanese name resulted in a minor coincidence: the vast underground world in EarthBound was originally known in Japanese as the chitei tairiku (\"continent at the depths of the earth\"). Given Toby's fondness for EarthBound and EarthBound's clear influence on Undertale as a whole, it almost feels like this translation choice was meant to be from the very start.",
        "raw": "On a side note, the decision to use chitei in the Japanese name resulted in a\nminor coincidence: the vast underground world in EarthBound was originally\nknown in Japanese as the chitei tairiku (\"continent at the depths of the earth\").\nGiven Toby's fondness for EarthBound and EarthBound's clear influence on\nUnderta/e as a whole, it almost feels like this translation choice was meant to be\nfrom the very start.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29714487,
          0.79597143,
          0.90686171,
          0.89927857
        ],
